# memory

Durable session + project memory for the chat front-end. Separate from the
prompt registry and from the deterministic benchmark path.

## Must
- Session transcripts live under `~/.luxe/sessions/<session_id>/` (`meta.json` +
  append-only `transcript.jsonl` + `fold.jsonl`), mirroring `run_state.py` idioms
- `gc_sessions` default eviction: keep the most recent 50 sessions AND drop
  anything older than 30 days
- `SessionMeta` evolves ADDITIVELY with defaulting fields only;
  `from_dict` filters unknown keys so old metas always load (and old code
  simply ignores new keys). 2026-07 additions: `backend_name` + `base_url`
  (multi-backend provenance, "" = predates the feature). Assistant transcript
  records are stamped `"backend": <name>`; readers (`resume._pair_turns`)
  ignore unknown record kinds AND unknown record keys — the transcript is
  append-only provenance, never a schema contract
- Project memory has two tiers with explicit confidence:
  - repo-local `<repo>/.luxe/memory.md` — user-curated, committable, priority,
    ALWAYS injected
  - `~/.luxe/memory/<project_hash>/facts.jsonl` — auto-captured, `confidence: auto`,
    NEVER injected until promoted to `confidence: manual`
  - `project_hash = sha256(abspath(repo_root))[:12]`
- `.luxe/memory.md` holds MACHINE-MANAGED FENCED BLOCKS alongside the user's
  own text (2026-08-04). The markers are LOAD-BEARING: `<!-- luxe:<name>
  begin … -->` … `<!-- luxe:<name> end -->`, currently `luxe:brief` (written
  by `luxe init`, gitkit/brief.py) and `luxe:notes` (written by session
  distillation, chat/notes.py). `splice_block` is the ONLY writer and the
  contract is absolute: RE-READ the file, replace only the region between
  that block's own markers, APPEND at end of file when absent (curated text
  therefore stays first — which is also `render_block`'s truncation
  priority), preserve every other byte, write via a temp file + rename, and
  never touch `facts.jsonl`. Callers cap their own payload in Python before
  splicing; a length instruction in a prompt is not a cap. The file remains
  the USER's — luxe adds to it, never owns it
- Memory is injected ONLY as the `<project_memory>` block inside `run_single`'s
  `extra_context`, NEVER by editing `PROMPT_REGISTRY` or the `system_prompt`
- `run_single`'s `extra_context` defaults to "" → byte-identical to legacy when
  no memory/conversation is present

## Must not
- Read or write `~/.claude/` (Claude Code's own memory)
- Read the repo-root `CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code's project-memory file; names are
  close enough to invite a refactor mistake)
- Touch `src/luxe/agents/prompts.py` or `src/luxe/agents/loop.py` (memory injects
  only via `run_single`'s `extra_context`, never the registry or the loop)

## Owns
- src/luxe/memory/**
